<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech CEZ posts CZK 8.4 bln 9month net.</title>
<headline>Czech CEZ posts CZK 8.4 bln 9month net.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for nine month period ending September 30 (in billions of crowns)</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit	 13.06     vs	13.1</p>
<p> After-tax		 8.4	vs	 7.4</p>
<p> Operating revenues   40.15     vs	36.12</p>
<p> Operating expenses   26.92     vs	22.91</p>
<p> Operating income     13.23     vs	13.20</p>
<p> Other expenses	  0.17     vs	 0.10</p>
<p> Total assets	 154.73	vs    131.02</p>
<p> Current assets	11.71	vs	8.59</p>
<p> Depreciatioon	  4.09	vs	3.35</p>
<p>Note. Full company name is CEZ a.s.. The firm is the country's largest generator of electricity. All results are calculated according to international accounting standards (IAS).</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
